<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Louis IV, Landgrave of Hesse-Marburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1537">1537</a>–<a href="/years/1604">1604</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Louis IV was Landgrave of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marburg">Marburg</a> from 1567 to 1604, the second son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-i-landgrave-of-hesse">Philip the Magnanimous</a>, who received about a quarter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a>, centred on Marburg and its university, in the division of 1567. A strict Lutheran, he defended orthodoxy against the Calvinist leanings of his brother in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>. He died childless, and the division of his lands between Hesse-Kassel and Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/darmstadt">Darmstadt</a> caused decades of conflict.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/louis-iv-landgrave-of-hesse-marburg.jpg" alt="Louis IV, Landgrave of Hesse-Marburg" width="320" height="400" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludwig_IV._-_Miniaturen_%E2%80%93_Bomann_Museum.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
